"2D game character attack animation, full body, front view. Make every motion big, bold and exaggerated, with strong clear poses that read instantly even on a tiny phone screen. A red-haired trickster god with two small curved dark horns, a long dark green coat with golden ornaments over dark leather armor and tall boots stands facing the viewer, holding a short curved golden dagger in each hand, lowered at his sides. Wind-up, the first third of a second: he sinks into a low crouch with his weight on his back leg and draws his right dagger back to his hip; the blade lights up with green fire. Release: he rises from the crouch onto his bent front leg, both feet staying on the same spot at the same distance from the camera, and makes one short fast diagonal slash close in front of his chest, from his shoulder down to his opposite hip; a short streak of green and golden fire follows the blade and fades at once. Recovery, the rest of the clip: he steps back, straightens, the dagger returns to his side and he settles into exactly the same pose as the first frame. The daggers stay close to his body. He moves like a living man, with natural weight shifts, bending knees and a supple spine; he never rotates rigidly like a figurine on a stand. He always faces the viewer and never shows his back. He never moves toward or away from the camera and his size in the frame stays the same. His whole body and both daggers stay inside the frame at all times. His body stays solid and fully visible in every frame. Static locked-off camera: no zoom, no pan, no shake. Keep the character design exactly identical in every frame. Plain flat solid gray background exactly as in the input image, unchanged for the whole video: no floor, no shadow, no smoke, no dust. Smooth, punchy, high-quality game animation; the last frame matches the first frame."
